#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302305 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119885 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e28bd3d9-649d-5cc3-a12e-e1f821caaf24" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "283c298b-9742-57ea-bd3e-91b19039b7fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300155} {:answer/id #uuid "3769a266-b400-5c85-802d-d27c18680008" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300230} {:answer/id #uuid "3ceb53f1-24cc-5b40-a3c1-d1fa17f87b65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300258} {:answer/id #uuid "96dd2d17-0520-510d-b232-b7585772c28a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300722} {:answer/id #uuid "b028918f-5597-5a96-9cfb-a914220e3b81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b028918f-5597-5a96-9cfb-a914220e3b81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300841} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc136613-04c4-5a55-b3e0-721f19fcb626" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301880}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24196412-03d6-5e5f-92de-8b242613ba34" :question/math-academy-id "q-32649" :question/problem "$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $C=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $C$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{33}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $C$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ \\,\\,1\\,\\, & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+1{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ \\,\\,1\\,\\, & -3 & 3 \\\\ \\,\\,0\\,\\, & -1 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{32}=-1$ and ${u}_{33}=7,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}\\cdot {u}_{33}=(-1)\\cdot 7=-7.\n$$"}]}
